-- FG circuit pilot S2s: port of Tools.ShippingChildCoreC onto the context-predicate bundles (RefLawsAOpsX / RefLawsATeleX); generated by a rename-only script (names + suffix X, `AdmCtx O.quiet` -> `O.adm`). No sorry/axiom/native_decide/TRUSTED/law.

/-! # The core entry keeps the cache half, at every depth

`core_tripleACX`: from `JQC O D`, the core entry
`synthesizeCombinationalCore declName [] false` ends in `JQC O D` on EVERY
outcome, exceptions in the class, at any depth `D`:
* at the limit the entry throws before changing anything (`O.frameT`/`O.excOk`);
* outermost (`D = 0`): 7 pures, 4 framed sets, the cache clear
  (`tripleC_clear'`: the cache half re-established from `{}`), 7 framed sets;
* nested (`D ≠ 0`): 7 framed reads (the saved maps), 7 framed sets, NO clear
  (the cache half is carried);
* then the depth bump toX `D + 1` (`tripleC_depthSet`), the body under
  `hbodyC`, and the `finally` (`finCX`: depth back toX `D` by
  `tripleC_depthModify`, the nested restore is seven framed sets).

`full_tripleACX`: the same for `synthesizeCombinational` (core, one env read,
pure post-processing). `hentryT_of_bodyX` / `hentry_of_bodyX` derive the
premises `hentryT` / `hentry` of Tools/ShippingChildCacheA.lean from
`hbodyC`; `synthesizeChild_realA'X`, `synthesizeChild_tripleC'X` and
`closeInstsM_realA'X` restate the cache endpoints with `hbodyC` in place of
them. -/

